{"file":{"content":"# H23a hardening (H1–H4 + certificate appendix) + cycle elimination (SRCE #42)\n\nPer dd_critique3 Phase D / dd_critique2 §3-§4: harden H23a into explicit H1–H4 modules with a\nper-Q certificate appendix, and write cycle elimination with explicit constants. Both done; SRCE\nmanuscript now 32pp clean, master doc 5pp clean.\n\n## TASK 1: full per-Q certificate computed (cert_full.c)\n\ncert_LQ.c only gave |C_Q|, primitivity, M_Q, and the directly-measured residue gap κ_Q. The\ncritique's certificate appendix needs the WIELANDT-MECHANISM constants. NEW tool `cert_full.c`\ncomputes for every Q=2^r3^s (r≤8,s≤3, 25 moduli + pure Q=3):\n- **C_Q** = primitive recurrent component = non-leaf odd residues = (Z/Q)^×, |C_Q|=φ(Q)\n  (=2^{r-1} for s=0, =2^r3^{s-1} for s≥1); strongly connected, period 1, UNIQUE recurrent SCC\n  (leaves x≡0 mod3 are sinks).\n- **Γ_Q={γ_2,γ_3}** named certificate cycles: γ_2 = 2-adic (+2) collision cycle (additive order\n  2^{r-1} on odd residues mod 2^r, Lean addOrderOf_two), present iff r≥2; γ_3 = 3-adic b-period\n  cycle (b-sum equidistributes mod 3^s via 2 primitive mod 3^{s+1}, Lean two_unit_pow3), iff s≥1.\n- **α_Q** = min positive row-normalized edge weight on C_Q (edge-mass lower bound) ≥ 0.014 on grid.\n- **Δ_Q** = min nontrivial character phase on Γ_Q = min(2sin(π/2^{r-1}) [r≥2], 2sin(π/3^s) [s≥1]).\n  The worst character is the highest-frequency additive one. Δ_Q DECREASES with r (e.g. 2sin(π/128)\n  =0.049 at Q=256) — honest fixed-Q gap shrinkage, no Q-uniformity claimed.\n- **η_Q** = α_Q(1-cos Δ_Q) = RIGOROUS but crude Wielandt gap, ≥1.9e-5 on grid (worst Q=256).\n  Versus directly-measured κ_Q≥0.99: gulf κ_Q≫η_Q is just Wielandt-bound slackness; BOTH positive\n  ⟹ no nontrivial character is a coboundary at any Q on the grid.\n- **M_Q** = (|C_Q|-1)²+1 Wielandt accessibility exponent (L-independent), up to 20450 (Q=432).\n- **L_0(Q)** = H(Q)+M^z_Q+3, H(Q)=⌈log2(2/η_Q)⌉ (floor making H1 correction <η_Q/2), M^z_Q≤12.83\n  bits bulk margin. L_0 ranges 18–33.\n- Q=2 (|C_Q|=1): VACUOUS, no nontrivial character, H23a trivial there.\n\n## TASK 2: H1–H4 modular structure + certificate appendix in manuscript\n\n- NEW §\"The four modules H1–H4\" before the Wielandt-trajectory paragraph: maps each module to its\n  named object + appendix constants. H1=exact-cocycle perturbation (lem:cocycle), H2=stabilisation\n  (lem:stab), H3=Wielandt accessibility M_Q (prop:stepCgap), H4=non-coboundary gap Δ_Q (prob:cob,\n  equality case). Assembly H1+H2+H3+H4 = prop:stepCgap ⟹ gap η_Q>0 uniform in L≥L_0(Q) ⟹ H23a.\n- NEW APPENDIX A \"The H23a finite certificate\" (\\appendix, label app:cert): per-Q table with\n  columns Q, (r,s), |C_Q|, Γ_Q, α_Q, Δ_Q, η_Q, M_Q, L_0, κ_Q (25 rows, grouped by r). Bulleted\n  description of each certificate object. Honest \"read across\": every η_Q>0, every κ_Q≥0.99, η_Q\n  decreases with r (high-freq 2-adic chars approach but never reach coboundary).\n- HONEST remaining: H1–H2 perturbation bookkeeping with explicit constants now in hand — finite-\n  dimensional, NOT a new arithmetic input. (Note: `\\input{}` inside tabular gave \"Misplaced\n  \\noalign\"; inlined the 25 rows directly — cleaner, self-contained, no external file dep.)\n\n## TASK 3: cycle elimination — ε-stability window made numerical\n\nRoute A was already reduced to prop:epsstab (ε-stable H23a/QSD under tilt s_b→s_b-ε). With M_Q now\ntabulated, added §\"The stability window is explicit, and no exceptional set survives the floor\":\n- Under tilt, each edge shifts z by ε; over a Wielandt path (length ≤M_Q) cumulative shift ≤εM_Q;\n  staying in bulk window (half-width m_Q bits, O(1) from QSD collapse) needs ε≤ε_0(Q)=m_Q/M_Q.\n- Needed tilt ε_x=log2(1+1/(3x))≤1/(3x ln2), decays like 1/x.\n- Worst grid M_Q=20450 (Q=432), conservative m_Q=3 bits ⟹ ε_0≥1.5e-4. At floor x=2^12,\n  ε_x=1.17e-4, ε_x M_Q≈2.4 bits already inside window ⟹ ε_x≤ε_0(Q) for ALL x≥2^12, NO exceptional\n  set above floor. At x~1e9 (relevant regime) ε_x~1e-10, slack 6 orders (ε_x M_Q~1e-6 bits).\n- Remaining: prop:epsstab's perturbation bookkeeping; its constants (M_Q,m_Q,α_Q) all tabulated.\n\n## Master doc updated\n\n- in:h23a openinput: certificate now \"computed explicitly\" + tabulated; H1–H4 modules listed;\n  ε_0(Q) window numerical. Remaining = H1–H2 bookkeeping.\n- Work tracker: H23a row → \"H1–H4 modularised; cert tabulated all Q | write H1–H2 perturbation\n  bookkeeping\"; Cycle elim → \"Route A ⟹ Prop epsstab; ε_0(Q) window explicit\".\n\n## Honest status (unchanged in kind)\n\nCollatz ⟸ FOUR open inputs. H23a: arithmetic core PROVED + Lean; certificate now EXPLICIT &\nuniform (all constants computed, η_Q>0 ∀Q on grid); H1–H4 modular; remaining = finite-dimensional\nH1–H2 perturbation bookkeeping (not arithmetic). Cycle elimination: Route A reduced to prop:epsstab\nwith explicit ε_0(Q) stability window covering all x≥2^12; remaining = the same finite perturbation\nstep. NEITHER fully closed — the unwritten finite-dimensional bookkeeping is real, not hand-waved.\nNOT a Collatz proof.\n\n## Artifacts\n- `c_scripts/cert_full.c` — full H23a certificate (C_Q,Γ_Q,α_Q,Δ_Q,η_Q,M_Q,L_0) all Q; emits\n  cert_full.txt + cert_full_table.tex.\n- `docs/stabilized_residue_extinction.tex` — §H1–H4 modules; Appendix A certificate (table inlined);\n  §ε-stability window. 32pp clean.\n- `docs/master_dependencies.tex` — in:h23a + tracker updated. 5pp clean.\n\n## Bottom line\nH23a hardened: the certificate $(\\mathcal C_Q,\\Gamma_Q,\\alpha_Q,\\Delta_Q,\\eta_Q,M_Q,L_0(Q))$ is now\ncomputed explicitly for all 25 moduli Q=2^r3^s (r≤8,s≤3) and tabulated in a new appendix; the proof\nis organised into four named modules H1–H4 (cocycle perturbation, stabilisation, Wielandt\naccessibility, non-coboundary gap) with the rigorous Wielandt gap η_Q=α_Q(1-cos Δ_Q)>0 at every Q\n(crude vs the directly-measured κ_Q≥0.99). Cycle elimination's ε-stability window is now numerical:\nε_0(Q)=m_Q/M_Q≥1.5e-4 covers all x≥2^12 with no